<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI28-RSH-003>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI28-RSH-003" ;
  triage:title "PeerSyncPolicy::validate() doesn't bound max_message_age — reachable panic in recovery worker" ;
  triage:description "PeerSyncPolicy::validate() accepts any operator-settable max_message_age value without enforcing reasonable bounds. If an operator configures an unreasonably large max_message_age (or in edge cases where the value is externally influenced), the recovery coordinator's worker thread can panic when performing DateTime - Duration subtraction (computing message-age thresholds in the backoff/recovery logic). This panic is unhandled in the worker thread, causing the entire recovery coordinator to terminate silently. This issue combines with AI28-RSH-002 (silent mutex poisoning) into a critical production failure mode: (1) an unbounded max_message_age triggers a panic in the worker thread, (2) the panic poisons the slot-tracking mutex, (3) slot state becomes permanently wedged at running=true with zero observability. An operator unable to restart the daemon or clear the state would experience permanent recovery loss for that peer. Fix required: validate max_message_age to ensure it does not overflow chrono::DateTime subtraction; recommend a maximum practical value (e.g., max 30 days or 2.5M seconds) and reject configurations that exceed it. Additionally, see AI28-RSH-002 for the complementary fix to handle mutex poisoning properly. Severity flagged as Important per gate criteria, but please prioritize in the fix round given the combination with RSH-002 into a real production-risk failure mode." ;
  triage:category "Service-Hardening" ;
  triage:severity "Important" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
